    const K_Y = [                                                      // the height on the trunk the gaze rests on, while it rests on the Old Stick
      [U_GAZE, 34],                                                    // 3 m past the hoop: the tower's lower tiers, the sun behind the trunk
      [uAtZ(LEE_Z), 44],                                               // the drift's lee edge, out of the wood: the tower stands open, the gaze climbs it
      [uAtZ(228), 40],                                                 // the course's knot at z 228, level over the shadow road
      [uAtZ(BZ0 - 24), 46],                                            // the course's knot 24 m before the barrel's mouth: the tower through the rings
      [U_EXIT, 40],                                                    // out of the last ring
      [uAtZ(HZ - 80), 34],                                             // the course's knot 80 m short of the trunk: the tips of the low curls ahead, the sun behind the trunk
      [U_NEAR, 36],                                                    // the pass under the skirts
      [U_ARC[0], 40]];                                                 // the start of the turn (by here the keyed gaze below has taken over)
    const K_LINE = [[U_NEAR, 0], [U_ARC[0], 1]];                       // 0 = the tower, 1 = the keyed gaze below: it leaves the trunk between the pass under the skirts and the start of the turn
    // The gaze of the swing and the last line (amendment 2): on the swing the aim keeps within 38 degrees of the light (piece B, below); on the last line the typed rows hold the gaze's bearing 0.66 and 0.60 radians (38 and 34 degrees) from the light's at the first quarter knot and the middle knot; with them, on a frame of 16:9 or wider, the sun and its
    // straw halo stay in the frame or at its edge and what we look at is shaving against the light. From the middle knot to the last quarter knot the gaze turns onto the line's own heading, 50 degrees off the sun's bearing, and the light goes to the frame's side, or past it where the frame is not wide enough. Bearing in radians from +Z toward +X
    // (the line heads 0.87, the sun stands at 0); elevation in radians. Each row at a knot of the course.
